A||||4||spideyfoot||HELP what is the trick for a rounded off sparkplug||||1||
Z||000000||spideyfoot||05-12-2001||04:40 PM||||Well I thought the plug was coming out but I guess I was rounding off the plugs nut area. It looks like these were the original plugs in my 113000 mile car. come on soomebody must know a trick.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Nashco||05-12-2001||11:09 PM||||Well, you didn't specify what engine or which plug it is, so I'll assume you have room to perform the following trick.  The best way to do it is to use a deep, thin walled, six point socket.  Using a 16mm socket, pound the socket on until it is on the same amount a regular socket would go on.  After you get it on, turn it forcibly, but gently; don't use any air tools or quick impact.  If the 16mm strips, try the next size down.  The 15mm might be very hard to get on, but if the 16 won't work, that's the best option.<P>Let me know if this works.  I'm not even sure which size plugs your car has, as I haven't changed my own plugs yet (I just got it).  This is a trick my dad told me, and he's probably changed spark plugs more times than you and I have driven a car, so this probably works <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>By the way, if you don't have a socket like this, go buy the 15 and 16 at Sears.  You can get the craftsman tools, which are cheap and guaranteed if they break.  You will want to get 3/8" drive, to achieve the thin wall.  Make sure it is 6 point also, as a 12 point will have less resitance to strip.<P>Good luck!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||ray b||05-12-2001||11:27 PM||||wd-40 or rust buster,but first try to remove trash gunk and rust so tool will fit all the way on the plug.shop vacume cleaner will work or air blaster to clean and clear out junk so tool fits on all the way.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Nashco||05-12-2001||11:43 PM||||Yeah, I didn't think to mention that, good thinking ray.  Make sure you get all that crap out of the plug area so you can get the tool on all the way.  After you clean it all out, letting some oil sit on it overnight would help a lot too.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||spideyfoot||05-13-2001||12:10 AM||||well its the # 3 plug on a 4 banger. Already removed the hood. Shot it with pb blaster started it. blasted it. Im trying to use smaller sockets havnt had any luck yet got it soaking overnight. It is a hard place to hammer on a socket. Right near the window on an upswing. If that dont work tom. I might try to carve out new edges with a moto tool. then its drilling and ezout time I guess. Which Im sure will lead to head pulling. so ive got all my Intak/exhaust head bolts soaking man I hope I dont have to resort to that||||reg||1
